# WASM editor

`sqyre-app` also builds for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with `--no-default-features` as a browser-only macro editor (import/export `db.yaml`; no Run, capture, OCR, hotkeys, tray, or overlays).

- Runtime code sits behind the `native-runtime` / `hooks` / `overlay-buttons` features or `#[cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))]`. New native deps go under `[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = "wasm32"))'.dependencies]` or an optional feature dep — never in the unconditional `[dependencies]` of `sqyre-app` or crates it always pulls in.
- Crates in the editor graph — `sqyre-domain`, `-varref`, `-ui-model`, `-ui-theme`, `-ports`, `-persist`, `-serialize`, `-validate`, `-hotkeys` (no `hooks`), `-overlay` (no `runtime`) — stay wasm-clean: no `std::thread`, `std::fs`, `std::process`, `std::env::{temp_dir,current_exe}` or OS APIs without a `#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]` split. Time via `web-time` (`std` `Instant`/`SystemTime::now` panic). RNG: keep workspace `uuid` `js`; a direct `getrandom` dep needs its wasm backend feature.
- Never block the browser main thread (no `block_on`/`pollster`, sync `rfd::FileDialog`, sleeps, busy-waits). `wasm_bindgen_futures::spawn_local`, stash the result, poll it in `update` — pattern in `wasm_io.rs`; file dialogs go through `file_dialogs.rs`.
- Panics/logs: `console_error_panic_hook` + `eframe::WebLogger` (`main.rs`). `eprintln!` (incl. `crate::log::warn`) is discarded in the browser.
- Hide or disable runtime-only UI on wasm rather than showing broken controls.
- Verify with `make wasm-check` (CI; `cargo check` only — no clippy/tests on wasm). `make wasm` → `bin/wasm/` for deploys; never ship `trunk serve`'s `dist/`.
